  "id": "law-of-contiguity",
  "term": "law of contiguity",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, the law of contiguity is the principle that mental impressions or ideas become linked when they have previously occurred together. Because of this connection, one idea tends to call up another that has coexisted with it in the mind.",
